<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:64:default:gcc">
<!--
    kuna issue `kuna-indirectonly` (P6, sub-stage merge-aggressiveness).

    An ILLEGAL INPUT is an input Varnode that ActionDirectWrite never reached,
    so nothing a formal parameter feeds can be responsible for its value: on a
    normal frame, the leftover contents of a stack slot the function overwrites
    before it reads.  Merge::mergeTestAdjacent refuses every speculative merge
    involving such a variable, and HighVariable::hasName refuses to name an
    unaffected input whose members are all of that kind.  Both refusals end
    "unless the illegal input is only used indirectly", and that exception needs
    the `indirectonly` Varnode flag, which nothing in kuna set:
    Funcdata::markIndirectOnly / checkIndirectUse (funcdata_varnode.cc:801-858)
    were unported and ActionMarkIndirectOnly was a documented no-op, so
    isIndirectOnly() answered false everywhere.

    Two functions, the same shape coreutils `date` -O0 `main` has (gcc frame, a
    `struct timespec` at -0xc0(%rbp) whose address escapes on the other branch,
    filled from one call result by a divide and a remainder).  `take` is the
    positive and `keep` is the counterexample:

      take:  push rbp / mov rbp,rsp / sub rsp,0x120
             mov eax,[c1] / test eax,eax / je 1f
             lea rax,[rbp-0xc0] / mov rdi,rax / mov rsi,[str] / call parse
             jmp 8f
      1:     call now_ns                      ; the value, in RAX
             mov [rbp-0xc8],rax
             mov rdi,1000000000
             ... idiv ... / mov [rbp-0xc0],rax ; when.tv_sec  = v / 1e9
             ... idiv ... / mov [rbp-0xb8],rdx ; when.tv_nsec = v % 1e9
      8:     lea rax,[rbp-0xc0] / mov rdi,rax / call use / leave / ret

      keep:  identical, with 1000000007 for the divisor and ONE extra
             instruction pair at the top:
             mov rsi,[rbp-0xb8] / mov [c2],rsi  ; a REAL read of the entry value

    `lea rbp-0xc0` escapes the struct, so both of its slots are address-tied.
    In `take` the value each holds on entry reaches nothing but the INDIRECTs of
    the two calls (indirect-only), and the COPY that writes the remainder into
    `when.tv_nsec` wants to merge RAX's HighVariable, which also carries the
    call's result, into that slot.  In `keep` the same slot's entry value is
    read straight into a global before anything else happens, so one genuine
    read fails checkIndirectUse for the whole def-set and the flag must NOT be
    set: an uninitialized value must not be merged into a real variable.

    Pass 1 (option indirectonly off): the merge is refused in both functions,
    the call result gets its own register local and the slot is assigned across.
    Pass 2 (option indirectonly on, the default): `take` merges: the call
    result is computed straight into `when.tv_nsec` and the register local is
    gone, and `keep` is byte-identical to pass 1.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x1024">

</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x1024" name="take"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x10a1" name="keep"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x112c" name="parse"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x1130" name="now_ns"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x1136" name="use"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>option indirectonly off</com>
  <com>lo fu take</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>lo fu keep</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>option indirectonly on</com>
  <com>lo fu take</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>lo fu keep</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="indirectonly #1: off assigns the remainder across into the escaped slot" min="1" max="1">v3 = v1 % 1000000000;</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="indirectonly #2: on folds the remainder back into that same slot" min="1" max="1">v2 %= 1000000000;</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="indirectonly #3: on computes the call result straight into the slot" min="1" max="1">v2 = now_ns\(\);</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="indirectonly #4: the call result spills to a register local in take pass 1 and in both passes of keep" min="3" max="3">v1 = now_ns\(\);</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="indirectonly #5: that register local is declared three times, never four" min="3" max="3">int8 v1; // rax</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="indirectonly #6: keep reads the slot's entry value for real, in both passes" min="2" max="2">dat_114d = v3;</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="indirectonly #7: so keep's remainder is assigned across in BOTH passes; a directly-read illegal input is never marked" min="2" max="2">v3 = v1 % 0x3b9aca07;</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
